WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.469
-How it works is you're going to
hit this button here,

00:00:03.469 --> 00:00:04.837
which really works.

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.907
It activates the opinion topic
generator.

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.742
It will land on a random topic
that relates to

00:00:09.742 --> 00:00:11.010
this time of year.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.878
Whatever it is, you have to give
your opinion on it.

00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:16.282
-Knee jerk?
-Yep. First thing.

00:00:16.282 --> 00:00:18.851
Doesn't have to be prepared.
Nothing.

00:00:18.851 --> 00:00:20.419
You ready?
-Okay. Yep.

00:00:20.419 --> 00:00:21.887
-Go ahead.

00:00:21.887 --> 00:00:26.926
[ Musical beeping plays ]

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:30.897
-Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer.
-Oh. You know what?

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:34.834
This is what pisses me off
about that.

00:00:34.834 --> 00:00:37.970
No, but for real, okay so
they're mean to him

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.872
and there's a foggy night.

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:42.174
I guess this is the first time
it's ever happened.

00:00:42.174 --> 00:00:44.643
And so Santa puts him in front,
I'm assuming,

00:00:44.643 --> 00:00:46.045
and he lights the way.

00:00:46.045 --> 00:00:48.548
And then they go, "then all the
reindeer loved him,

00:00:48.548 --> 00:00:51.151
and they shouted out with glee,
Rudolph the Red-Nosed Reindeer,

00:00:51.151 --> 00:00:52.719
you'll go down in history."

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:58.858
First off, you don't just erase
the abuse.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.493
And secondly,
"you'll go down in history,"

00:01:01.493 --> 00:01:05.331
That's a claim. And fame and
love, I hate to say it,

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:08.268
but fame is not love.
They are very different things.

00:01:08.268 --> 00:01:11.938
I have done a lot of work to get
to that conclusion.

00:01:11.938 --> 00:01:14.808
And I hope Rudolph
sees a therapist.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:18.677
[ Bell dings ]
-That's unbelievable.

00:01:18.677 --> 00:01:20.813
[ Cheers and applause ]
-I never thought about that.

00:01:20.813 --> 00:01:21.948
That is fantastic.

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.683
-I've never
thought about it either.

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:26.285
-That's so good. That's the
whole point of the game.

00:01:26.285 --> 00:01:27.920
Let's give it another go
over here.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:29.488
-Okay. All right.

00:01:29.488 --> 00:01:35.361
[ Musical beeping plays ]

00:01:35.361 --> 00:01:41.367
-Mistletoe. If any decoration
needs to be me too'd,

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:48.274
the mistletoe -- this is the
most -- who the hell?

00:01:48.274 --> 00:01:52.445
Like, in what world -- like
walking through a doorway

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:55.247
with another person
weird enough.

00:01:55.247 --> 00:02:00.553
I don't need this perverted
garnish over the door.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.856
I don't want to see it.
I don't want to hear about it.

00:02:03.856 --> 00:02:07.026
-Oh, my God. I've never --
That's fantastic.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:10.129
I've never heard you
raise your voice.

00:02:10.129 --> 00:02:14.067
-It's an upsetting garnish.
-It's an upsetting, yeah.

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:17.603
Let's do another one.
-Okay. All right.

00:02:17.603 --> 00:02:23.876
[ Musical beeping plays ]

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:27.546
-Fingerless gloves.
-Okay.

00:02:27.546 --> 00:02:31.217
They seem to be favored by
crooks in movies.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.584
[ Laughter ]

00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:37.990
Now, I'm no forensic scientist,
but I would imagine

00:02:37.990 --> 00:02:41.728
that it's exactly these parts of
the hand that you want to

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:44.663
cover up if you're a crook.
-There you go.

00:02:44.663 --> 00:02:45.765
Listen up, crooks.
-Alright.

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:50.369
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.369 --> 00:02:52.638
-I want to do this all night.
We only have time for one more.

00:02:52.638 --> 00:02:56.275
-I love my own thoughts.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:56.275 --> 00:02:59.345
-John, you have one more.
-Okay, go.

00:02:59.345 --> 00:03:02.181
-Thank you very much.
Here we go.

00:03:02.181 --> 00:03:03.849
-yeah.

00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:09.956
[ Musical beeping plays ]

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:12.525
-The 2010s. 2010s.
-Oh, they're ending.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:14.960
-They are, the decade is over.
-Ooh!

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:16.128
[ Audience groans ]
-That's right.

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:20.667
-Well, what a decade.

00:03:20.667 --> 00:03:22.534
Here's how I'd sum up the 2010s.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:25.804
I was going through the airport
and there was a guy

00:03:25.804 --> 00:03:28.874
and he was traveling and there
was a woman from TSA.

00:03:28.874 --> 00:03:30.843
And they were screaming
at each other.

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:34.547
And she said,
"I wouldn't disrespect you,

00:03:34.547 --> 00:03:37.183
if you hadn't disrespected me
in the first place."

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:41.688
And that is the 2010s.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:44.456
We're trying to figure out who
disrespected who

00:03:44.456 --> 00:03:48.194
in the first place and we're
both screaming at each other

00:03:48.194 --> 00:03:51.697
and everyone is just trying to
get on their Southwest flight.

00:03:51.697 --> 00:03:53.699
-That's fantastic.

00:03:53.699 --> 00:03:55.335
That is John Mulaney
right there.

